/target
# The shippable output. `dist/bundle` is the 17-file engine folder, `dist/*.exe` is the ONE
# file a person downloads. Built artifacts, never committed; a GitHub release carries them.
/dist/
# CI points CEF_PATH at the workspace; never let 171 MB of engine near git.
/.cef/
/probe-report.jsonl
/probe-profile
/app-window.png
*.log
/tools/*.png
/tools/wpn-copy.db*
/bench-profiles

# The bundled engines. `runtime/firefox` is a real Firefox, 345 MB, downloaded by
# tools/get-firefox.ps1; the Chromium one is downloaded by the cef crate into
# ~/.local/share/cef and never lives here. Neither belongs in git: they are third-party
# binaries with their own licences, and one `git add -A` would put a browser in the history
# forever.
/runtime/

# Bench artefacts. The .jsonl rows are the measurements and ARE kept; the per-run stdout and
# stderr are scratch, and there is one pair per run.
/tools/bench-*.out
/tools/bench-*.err
/tools/probe-*.out
/tools/probe-*.err
/tools/login-*.out
/tools/login-*.err
/tools/*.out
/tools/*.err

# ⛔ PUBLIC REPO: the to-do list is not published (owner directive, 2026-08-29).
# These notes are the most candid writing in the repo - what is broken, what is half-built, what is
# waiting on a person - and Odin's Loki files them here automatically from chat history. The
# folder's own README stays tracked (it is already tracked, and it states the convention); only the
# items are ignored. Managed by public_todo_guard.py in the Odin repo.
/docs/todo/*
!/docs/todo/README.md
